   "id": "cara-simpan-dan-cek-live-preview",
   "langs": {
    "id": {
     "title": "Cara Menyimpan File dan Mengecek Live Preview",
     "desc": "Tata cara menyimpan HTML, CSS, dan JS di editor Clincoo lalu memastikan preview menampilkan versi terbaru, bukan cache lama.",
     "content": "<p class=\"mb-4\">Di <a href=\"https://editor.clincoo.buzz/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"underline decoration-gray-300 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-gray-900 text-gray-900\">editor.clincoo.buzz</a>, perubahan baru tampil di preview setelah file disimpan. Titik di tab atau tanda belum tersimpan berarti browser masih menjalankan salinan lama.</p><h2 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-2\">Simpan file yang sedang dibuka</h2><ol class=\"list-decimal pl-6 mb-4 space-y-1\"><li class=\"mb-1\">Selesai mengedit, tekan simpan atau pintasan Ctrl+S (Command+S di Mac).</li><li class=\"mb-1\">Tunggu tab kehilangan tanda belum tersimpan sebelum menilai tampilan.</li><li class=\"mb-1\">Kalau kamu mengubah CSS di file terpisah, simpan file itu juga — menyimpan HTML saja tidak menulis ulang stylesheet.</li></ol><h2 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-2\">Muat ulang preview dengan benar</h2><p class=\"mb-4\">Kalau warna atau teks tidak berubah, muat ulang panel preview. Untuk CSS yang bandel, hard reload di browser (Ctrl+Shift+R) membersihkan cache preview. Jangan menyalin aturan yang sama ke dua file; browser memakai yang terakhir dimuat dan hasilnya terlihat acak.</p><h2 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-2\">Cek lebar yang dipakai pengunjung</h2><ul class=\"list-disc pl-6 mb-4 space-y-1\"><li class=\"mb-1\">Desktop: sekitar 1280px, pastikan navigasi tidak terpotong.</li><li class=\"mb-1\">Ponsel: sekitar 390px, pastikan teks tidak meluber ke samping.</li><li class=\"mb-1\">Kalau hanya satu lebar yang rusak, catat lebarnya sebelum minta bantuan.</li></ul><p class=\"mb-4\">Biasakan satu perubahan, satu simpan, satu cek. Pola itu membuat regresi mudah diurutkan mundur.</p>",
     "source": "MDN Web Docs — CSS first steps",
     "sourceUrl": "https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn/CSS/First_steps",
     "sourceSnippet": "CSS is used to style and lay out web pages.",
     "source2": "Clincoo Editor",
     "source2Url": "https://editor.clincoo.buzz/",
     "source3": "Clincoo App",
     "source3Url": "https://app.clincoo.buzz/"
    },
    "en": {
     "title": "How to Save a File and Check Live Preview",
     "desc": "How to save HTML, CSS, and JS in the Clincoo editor and make sure the preview shows the latest version, not an old cache.",
     "content": "<p class=\"mb-4\">In <a href=\"https://editor.clincoo.buzz/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"underline decoration-gray-300 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-gray-900 text-gray-900\">editor.clincoo.buzz</a>, a change shows in the preview only after the file is saved. A dot on the tab or an unsaved mark means the browser is still running the old copy.</p><h2 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-2\">Save the file you have open</h2><ol class=\"list-decimal pl-6 mb-4 space-y-1\"><li class=\"mb-1\">When the edit is done, press save or the Ctrl+S shortcut (Command+S on a Mac).</li><li class=\"mb-1\">Wait until the tab loses the unsaved mark before you judge the layout.</li><li class=\"mb-1\">If you edited CSS in a separate file, save that file too — saving the HTML does not rewrite the stylesheet.</li></ol><h2 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-2\">Reload the preview the right way</h2><p class=\"mb-4\">If a color or sentence does not change, reload the preview panel. For stubborn CSS, a hard reload (Ctrl+Shift+R) clears the preview cache. Do not copy the same rule into two files; the browser uses whichever loads last, and the result looks random.</p><h2 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-2\">Check the widths visitors actually use</h2><ul class=\"list-disc pl-6 mb-4 space-y-1\"><li class=\"mb-1\">Desktop: about 1280px, and make sure the nav is not cut off.</li><li class=\"mb-1\">Phone: about 390px, and make sure text does not overflow sideways.</li><li class=\"mb-1\">If only one width breaks, note that width before you ask for help.</li></ul><p class=\"mb-4\">Get used to one change, one save, one check. That pattern makes a regression easy to undo.</p>",
     "source": "MDN Web Docs — CSS first steps",
     "sourceUrl": "https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn/CSS/First_steps",
     "sourceSnippet": "CSS is used to style and lay out web pages.",
     "source2": "Clincoo Editor",
     "source2Url": "https://editor.clincoo.buzz/",
     "source3": "Clincoo App",
     "source3Url": "https://app.clincoo.buzz/"
    }
   }
